    "width": 412.6,
    "height": 9
   },
   {
    "str": "Questions and Writing for Northwestern University",
    "x": 60,
    "y": 704,
    "width": 337.61,
    "height": 14
   },
   {
    "str": "Why are you interested in this college? (Made-up prompt, up to 300 words.)",
    "x": 60,
    "y": 678.4,
    "width": 393.63,
    "height": 11
   },
   {
    "str": "I want to study engineering somewhere that treats a wrong answer as the start of the work. When I",
    "x": 60,
    "y": 657,
    "width": 479.34,
    "height": 11
   },
   {
    "str": "read about design projects in the first year at Northwestern, I recognized the way our robotics team",
    "x": 60,
    "y": 641.6,
    "width": 480.55,
    "height": 11
   },
   {
    "str": "works: build something rough, test it on the real field, and fix what breaks. As co-captain of my soccer",
    "x": 60,
    "y": 626.2,
    "width": 492.77,
    "height": 11
   },
   {
    "str": "team, I have learned that a group improves fastest when everyone is allowed to point out a problem,",
    "x": 60,
    "y": 610.8,
    "width": 486.68,
    "height": 11
   },
   {
    "str": "and I want classmates who do that. I also hope to keep tutoring, because explaining an idea is the",
    "x": 60,
    "y": 595.4,
    "width": 476.32,
    "height": 11
   },
   {
    "str": "quickest way I know to find out whether I understand it.",
    "x": 60,
    "y": 580,
    "width": 267.19,
    "height": 11
   }
  ]
 ]
}
